  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Computing Jacobian Determinant for Given Transformations</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given the following transformations of \(x\) and \(y\) such that \(\displaystyle x={@eq1@}\) and \(\displaystyle y={@eq2@}\). 
Compute its Jacobian as shown below:</p>
<p>We will take the determinant of the two by two matrix of partial derivatives using the formula;</p>
\( \displaystyle \frac{\partial(x,y) }{\partial(u,v) }= \displaystyle \begin{vmatrix}
\displaystyle \frac{\partial x}{\partial u} &  \displaystyle \frac{\partial x}{\partial v}\\
\displaystyle \frac{\partial y}{\partial u} & \displaystyle \frac{\partial y}{\partial v}
\end{vmatrix}\)
<br>\(\quad\quad=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]
<br>
<p>\(\quad\quad=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>Given the following transformations of \(x\) and \(y\) such that \(\displaystyle x={@eq1@}\) and \(\displaystyle y={@eq2@}\). </p>
<p>There really isn’t much to do here other than compute the Jacobian as shown;</p>
<p>We will take the determinant of the two by two matrix of partial derivatives using the formula;</p>
\(\displaystyle\frac{\partial(x,y) }{\partial(u,v) }=\begin{vmatrix}
\displaystyle\frac{\partial x}{\partial u} &  \displaystyle \frac{\partial x}{\partial v}\\
\displaystyle\frac{\partial y}{\partial u} & \displaystyle \frac{\partial y}{\partial v}
\end{vmatrix}\)
<p>To find the partial derivatives, we have:</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle
\frac{\partial x}{\partial u} = {@aa@} \quad \text{and} \quad \displaystyle \frac{\partial x}{\partial v} = {@bb@}
\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle
\frac{\partial y}{\partial u} = {@cc@} \quad \text{and} \quad \displaystyle \frac{\partial y}{\partial v} = {@dd@}
\)</p>
<p>Now, we can form the Jacobian matrix:</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle \quad\quad={@ta1@}\)</p>
<p>Calculating the determinant:</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle
\frac{\partial(x,y)}{\partial(u,v)} = ({@aa@} \times {@dd@}) - ({@cc@} \times {@bb@}) = {@ta2@}
\)</p>
<p>Therefore, the Jacobian determinant is \({@ta2@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
